---
layout: app-shell.njk
permalink: /
title: "Home | Stefanos Tzortzoglou"
bodyScripts:
  - src: "/scripts/app.js"
    type: "module"
  - src: "/scripts/contact-widget.js"
    type: "module"
  - src: "/scripts/palette.js"
    type: "module"
  - src: "/scripts/departures.js"
    type: "module"
  - src: "/scripts/f1.js"
    type: "module"
bodyClass: "bg-brand-bg text-brand-text antialiased min-h-screen flex flex-col"
shell: true
navDrawerOnly: true
signOut: true
---
<section class="app-page">

  {% include "chrome/weather-icons.njk" %}

  {# The hero.

     `data-wx` is set by app.js from the same describe() call that picks the chip's icon, so the
     card's weather and the chip's weather are the same fact rendered twice rather than two
     guesses. Until the forecast lands it is "unknown", which draws the plain surface - a card
     that guesses sunshine and corrects itself to rain is worse than one that simply waits. #}
  {# Four layers, painted in this order behind the text: the sky and what hangs in it, the city,
     what falls past the city, and a scrim that gives the text column its contrast back. All four
     are decoration and none of them is reachable - the chip says the weather in words, and the
     skyline says nothing the place name beside it does not already say. #}
  <div id="hero" class="hero" data-wx="unknown">
    <div class="hero-sky" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    {# The skyline of wherever the forecast is for, computed by the API from OpenStreetMap
       building heights and delivered as integers, never as markup - app.js bounds-checks them
       and builds the `d` itself. `data-city` on the card fades the layer in, so nothing appears
       until there is a real city to show, and nothing at all appears for a place with no
       skyline worth drawing. `slice` rather than `meet`: the box is narrower than the art, so
       it crops the sides and keeps the full height - the frame is already centred on the
       tallest thing, which is what the crop is guaranteed to keep. #}
    <div class="hero-city" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1200 120" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMax slice" focusable="false">
        <path id="cityArt" fill="currentColor"></path>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-fall" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="hero-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="hero-body">
      <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
        {# Non-breaking space so the line exists before the name does and nothing below it
           moves when the greeting arrives. #}
        <h1 id="greeting" class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-text">&nbsp;</h1>

        {# One sentence composed from what the app already knows. Each clause that refers to a
           queue is a link to the queue, because a number you cannot act on is decoration.
           Empty until there is something true to say. #}
        <p id="digest" class="hero-digest"></p>
      </div>

<div id="wx" class="relative w-full sm:w-auto" data-open="false">
      <button id="wxChip" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="wxPanel"
        class="wx-chip w-full sm:w-auto">
        <svg id="wxChipIcon" class="h-8 w-8 shrink-0 text-brand-accent" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <use href="#wx-cloud"></use>
        </svg>
        <span class="text-left leading-tight min-w-0">
          <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-brand-text">
            <span id="wxChipTemp" class="tabular-nums">—</span><span id="wxChipWhat" class="font-normal text-brand-muted"></span>
          </span>
          <span class="block text-xs text-brand-muted truncate">
            <span id="wxChipPlace"></span><span id="wxChipTime" class="tabular-nums"></span>
          </span>
        </span>
        <span class="sr-only">Show the full forecast</span>
      </button>

      <div id="wxPanel" class="wx-panel" role="group" aria-label="Full forecast">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
          <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-brand-text">Weather</h2>
          <p id="weatherPlace" class="text-xs text-brand-muted"></p>
        </div>

        {# One live region for the whole panel: loading, the forecast, and any failure all land
           here, so a screen reader is told once rather than on every field. #}
        <div id="weather" role="status" aria-live="polite">
          <p class="text-sm text-brand-muted">Loading the forecast…</p>
        </div>

        {# Shown only when the browser has the API, and never prompting on its own: an
           unexplained permission dialog on page load is the one thing everybody refuses by
           reflex. The button says what it will do; the browser then asks. #}
        <div id="geo" class="mt-5 border-t border-brand-border pt-4 hidden">
          <p id="geoNote" class="text-xs text-brand-muted"></p>
          <button type="button" id="geoBtn" class="btn-secondary text-sm px-4 py-1.5 mt-3">Use my location</button>
        </div>
      </div>{# /#wxPanel #}
    </div>{# /#wx #}
    </div>{# /.hero-body #}
  </div>{# /.hero #}

  {# --- the way to everything -------------------------------------------
     The two admin tiles carry data-min-role and are hidden until shell.js confirms the role,
     exactly like the rail - so the grid never offers a tile that answers 403. #}
  <h2 class="sr-only">Shortcuts</h2>
  <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <li class="hidden" data-min-role="Admin">
      <a href="/admin/accounts/" class="tile">
        {% icon "fa-solid-users", "tile-icon" %}
        <span class="tile-count" id="tilePending" data-loading="1">—</span>
        <span class="tile-label">Awaiting approval</span>
      </a>
    </li>
    <li class="hidden" data-min-role="Admin">
      <a href="/admin/messages/" class="tile">
        {% icon "fa-solid-envelope-open-text", "tile-icon" %}
        <span class="tile-count" id="tileUnread" data-loading="1">—</span>
        <span class="tile-label">Unread messages</span>
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/profile/" class="tile">
        {% icon "fa-solid-user-gear", "tile-icon" %}
        <span class="tile-count tile-count--none" aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;</span>
        <span class="tile-label">Your profile</span>
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  {# --- departures --------------------------------------------------------
     On screen from the first paint, holding its own space, and removed entirely if it turns out
     to have nothing to say. A card that announces itself and then admits it knows
     nothing is worse than no card, and this one is useless to anybody whose API has no key.

     It does not poll. The API caches for 45 seconds and the whole deployment shares 100 requests
     per 15 minutes, so a tab left open on a timer would quietly spend that on nobody reading it.
     It refreshes when you come back to the tab and the numbers have gone stale, and when asked. #}
  <section id="departures" aria-labelledby="dep-heading" class="mt-8" data-card="loading">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-1 mb-1">
      {# The icon leads, and it is the same one /transit/ leads with - so this card reads as a
         preview of that page rather than as a different thing about buses. The operator moved
         down to the stop line, where the other facts the board reports already are. #}
      <h2 id="dep-heading" class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-bold text-brand-text">
        {% icon "fa-solid-bus", "h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-brand-accent" %}
        <span>Next departures</span>
      </h2>
      {# The stop name and the controls are two lines rather than one wrapping line.

         As one line they fitted beside the heading while the name was empty and wrapped the
         moment it arrived, so the three controls dropped a row under the reader's pointer - 32px
         of the home view's remaining shift. Two lines are two lines whatever the stop is called,
         which is the point: Portalgatan and Stockholm Centralstation now cost the same height.

         The name's own line is held open by a placeholder bar, because an empty span reserves
         nothing. setting textContent replaces it, the same way the lists work. #}
      <div class="text-sm text-brand-muted md:flex md:items-end md:gap-x-2">
        <p class="min-h-5">
          <span id="depStop"><span class="skel inline-block h-4 w-40 align-middle" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span id="depOperator"></span><span id="depAge" class="tabular-nums"></span>
        </p>
        <p class="-ml-1.5 md:ml-0">
          <button type="button" id="depChange" class="link-action">Change stop</button>
          <button type="button" id="depRefresh" class="link-action ml-1">Refresh</button>
          <a href="/transit/" class="link-action ml-1 text-brand-accent">Full board</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      {# The picker, closed until asked for. A search box that is always there would be the
         loudest thing on a card whose job is to be glanceable. #}
      <form id="depPicker" method="get" class="hidden mb-4 border-b border-brand-border pb-4">
        <label for="depSearch" class="field-label text-sm">Search for a stop</label>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <input type="text" id="depSearch" name="depSearch" autocomplete="off" maxlength="80"
            placeholder="Portalgatan" class="field flex-1 min-w-[12rem]">
          <button type="submit" class="btn-primary text-sm">Search</button>
          <button type="button" id="depCancel" class="btn-secondary text-sm">Cancel</button>
        </div>
        <ul id="depResults" class="mt-3 space-y-1"></ul>
        <p id="depPickNote" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="hint mt-2"></p>
      </form>

      {# Placeholder rows, in the markup rather than drawn by script: they have to exist at
         first paint, and a skeleton that waits for JavaScript reserves nothing during the wait
         it is there for. render() clears the list, so these disappear when the board arrives. #}
      <ul id="depList" aria-busy="true" class="divide-y divide-brand-border">
        {%- for i in range(0, 5) %}
        <li class="skel-row" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="skel h-6 w-7 shrink-0"></span>
          <span class="skel h-4 flex-1"></span>
          <span class="skel h-4 w-12 shrink-0"></span>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      <p id="depNote" class="text-sm text-brand-muted"></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {# --- the next race weekend ---------------------------------------------
     On screen from the first paint, and removed if the season has no race left. Every time below
     is rendered from an ISO instant in the reader's
     own timezone by the browser, which is the only thing that knows what that is. #}
  <section id="f1" aria-labelledby="f1-heading" class="mt-8" data-card="loading">
    <div class="mb-1 sm:flex sm:flex-wrap sm:items-end sm:justify-between sm:gap-x-4 sm:gap-y-1">
      {# The chequered flag rather than an "F1" badge, for the same reason as the bus above: it
         is the icon /f1/ itself leads with, so the two home cards and the two pages they preview
         all say the same thing the same way. It also stops one heading leading with a coloured
         box while the other trailed one. #}
      <h2 id="f1-heading" class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-bold text-brand-text">
        {% icon "fa-solid-flag-checkered", "h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-brand-accent" %}
        <span>Next race weekend</span>
      </h2>
      {# Stacked below sm for the same reason as the departures card: the location arriving is
         what wraps this row, and it arrives on every load. #}
      <div class="text-sm text-brand-muted sm:flex sm:items-end sm:gap-x-2">
        <p class="min-h-5"><span id="f1Where"><span class="skel inline-block h-4 w-28 align-middle" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></p>
        <p class="-ml-1.5 sm:ml-0">
          <a href="/f1/" class="link-action text-brand-accent">The season</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
        <h3 id="f1Name" class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">&nbsp;</h3>
        <span id="f1Sprint" class="hidden rounded-full bg-brand-accent/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-[11px] font-semibold text-brand-accent">Sprint weekend</span>
      </div>
      <p id="f1Countdown" class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted">&nbsp;</p>
      <ul id="f1Sessions" aria-busy="true" class="mt-4 divide-y divide-brand-border">
        {%- for i in range(0, 5) %}
        <li class="skel-row" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="skel h-5 flex-1"></span>
          <span class="skel h-5 w-24 shrink-0"></span>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

</section>
